{"name":"Tilled Soil","hex":"#6b4d35","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tilled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of till"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["ploughed or cultivated"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilled"},{"term":"soil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of mineral particles and organic material, used to support plant growth.","The unconsolidated mineral or organic material on the immediate surface of the earth that serves as a natural medium for the growth of land plants."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make dirty.","To become dirty or soiled."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tillage","blocks":[{"text":"Tillage is the agricultural preparation of soil by mechanical agitation of various types, such as digging, stirring, and overturning. Examples of human-powered tilling methods using hand tools include shoveling, picking, mattock work, hoeing, and raking. Examples of draft-animal-powered or mechanized work include ploughing, rototilling, rolling with cultipackers or other rollers, harrowing, and cultivating with cultivator shanks (teeth)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Tillage.jpg/330px-Tillage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tillage","wikidata":"Q878333"},{"title":"Soil","blocks":[{"text":"Soil, also commonly referred to as earth, is a mixture of organic matter, minerals, gases, water, and organisms that together support the life of plants and soil organisms. Some scientific definitions distinguish dirt from soil by restricting the former term specifically to displaced soil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Stagnogley.JPG/330px-Stagnogley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil","wikidata":"Q36133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tilling with Hungarian Grey cattle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg/500px-Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg/1280px-Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg/500px-Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rice tillage. Valencian Museum of Ethnology.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_(26462086444).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2DU_Kenya115_%285366706027%29.jpg/500px-2DU_Kenya115_%285366706027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2DU_Kenya115_%